# Cloudflare API credentials for deploy/scripts/configure-cloudflare-tunnel.sh
# and deploy/scripts/configure-cloudflare-managed-challenge.sh.
# Copy to /etc/uwe/cloudflare.env (chmod 600, root:uwe) — never commit real tokens.
#
# Required API token permissions:
#   - Account → Cloudflare One Connectors → Edit (or Cloudflare Tunnel → Edit)
#   - Zone → DNS → Edit (zone: uweanddragons.org)
#   - Zone → Zone WAF → Edit (zone: uweanddragons.org) — Managed Challenge only
#
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=your_token_here
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=2900c1e1ac39ce228f3b0a88bd83558f
# CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_ID=7760201a-52f9-4a48-aae8-eeea2845c65a
#
# Zone ID of the UWE domain — only needed for the Managed Challenge, and only
# when it is not already stored in UWE (System → Cloudflare).
# CLOUDFLARE_ZONE_ID=your_zone_id_here
#
# configure-cloudflare-tunnel.sh only ever writes the Studio (:3000) / Portal
# (:3001) ingress. The owner-only Brain surface (:3002) is never added
# automatically: check-cloudflare-tunnel.sh fails on a Brain ingress unless the
# deliberate opt-in BRAIN_PUBLIC_TUNNEL=1 is set (ADR 004/007). Brain enforces
# the `owner` role on every route; enable 2FA on that account before publishing.
# BRAIN_PUBLIC_TUNNEL=1
